most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system. That left us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-good version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again and it finished in all regions.\n- After the second attempt, health checks pass in all three regions and the error rate is 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway. I didn't retry, so on-call was paged only once.\n- The summary covers the failed release, both rollback attempts and the current state. It also lists three follow-ups:\n  1. Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.\n  2. Find out why v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also failing in staging.\n  3. Look into the deployment-system error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}